  "prompt": "Security report: data migrations reach into other groups, and an archive can unpack to any size.\n\n1. Group scoping. A migration archive (POST /api/groups/migrations) can carry ids from another group. A recipe tool given with another group's tool id is linked by that id and overwritten: that tool moves into the importing group and is renamed. An ingredient's sub-recipe reference (referencedRecipe) naming another group's recipe, by id or slug, links and exposes that recipe. Seen with the Mealie alpha and Nextcloud migrations.\n\nExpected: migrated recipes get the same group checks as the single-recipe zip import (POST /api/recipes/create/zip). Another group's tool keeps its group and name; the recipe gets a tool of the importing group instead (found there by id or slug, or created from the given name), with a different id. A sub-recipe reference is kept only when its id is a recipe of the importing group; otherwise referencedRecipe is null. The recipe itself still imports.\n\n2. Archive size. Migrations unpack the uploaded zip with no limit. Add to the migration utilities module (the one holding import_image, scrape_image and safe_local_path):\n- MAX_EXTRACTED_ARCHIVE_SIZE, the most one migration may unpack: 5 GiB (5,368,709,120 bytes);\n- ArchiveTooLargeError, a ValueError subclass;\n- extract_zip(archive, dest, max_size=None): unpacks the zip into dest and returns the bytes unpacked, the sum of the members' uncompressed sizes (members of 5 and 3 bytes give 8; a total equal to max_size is allowed). max_size defaults to MAX_EXTRACTED_ARCHIVE_SIZE, looked up when called. Over the limit it raises ArchiveTooLargeError before writing anything; dest is not even created.\nEvery migration that reads a zip honours the limit, and zips nested in an export (Cook'n, Tandoor) count toward the same total. The tests patch MAX_EXTRACTED_ARCHIVE_SIZE on that module to 1024, so migrators must read it at run time. A migration over the limit still answers 200; its report has status \"failure\" and exactly one entry, with the message \"Archive is too large to import\".\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/integration_tests/recipe_migration_tests tests/unit_tests/services_tests` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
  "title": "fix: scope migration imports to the group and limit archive size (#8761)",
